Prefetching a partially materialized tree artifact can hide a child that was already available through a directory symlink, then fail while restoring output permissions.

This focused test in ActionInputPrefetcherTestBase reproduces the failure in RemoteActionInputFetcherTest at b353e093a7df2cc4a10a10faf3a702a3b3f1c951:

```java
  @Test
  public void prefetchFiles_treeFiles_directorySymlink_partiallyMaterialized() throws Exception {
    Map<ActionInput, FileArtifactValue> metadata = new HashMap<>();
    Map<HashCode, byte[]> cas = new HashMap<>();
    ImmutableMap<String, String> contents =
        ImmutableMap.of(
            "alias/a/file", "content1",
            "alias/b/file", "content2",
            "target/a/file", "content1",
            "target/b/file", "content2");
    Pair<SpecialArtifact, ImmutableList<TreeFileArtifact>> treeAndChildren =
        createRemoteTreeArtifact(
            "dir", /* localContentMap= */ ImmutableMap.of(), contents, metadata, cas);
    SpecialArtifact tree = treeAndChildren.getFirst();
    Path existingFile = tree.getPath().getRelative("target/a/file");
    existingFile.getParentDirectory().createDirectoryAndParents();
    FileSystemUtils.writeContent(existingFile, UTF_8, "content1");
    tree.getPath().getChild("alias").createSymbolicLink(PathFragment.create("target"));

    AbstractActionInputPrefetcher prefetcher = createPrefetcher(cas);

    // The first alias child is already visible through the symlink. Preparing the next child's
    // directory must not make it disappear.
    wait(
        prefetcher.prefetchFilesInterruptibly(
            action, treeAndChildren.getSecond(), metadata::get, Priority.MEDIUM, Reason.INPUTS));

    for (Map.Entry<String, String> entry : contents.entrySet()) {
      assertThat(FileSystemUtils.readContent(tree.getPath().getRelative(entry.getKey()), UTF_8))
          .isEqualTo(entry.getValue());
    }
    assertTreeReadableNonWritableAndExecutable(tree.getPath());
  }
```

The presence check for alias/a/file succeeds through the symlink. Preparing the directory for alias/b/file replaces that symlink with a regular directory, making alias/a/file unreachable. DirectoryTracker.setOutputPermissions then throws FileNotFoundException for /exec/root/dir/alias/a while trying to restore permissions.

Every recorded child should remain readable with its recorded contents, and prefetch should complete with the normal output permissions. A repair also needs to respect recorded contents when an existing on-disk symlink no longer matches the tree metadata.

The reproduction runs in Bazel's InMemoryFileSystem on Linux. The tested source was compiled using Bazel 9.3.1. The introducing commit is unknown. This belongs to Remote Execution.

#21171 concerned directory contents missing from tree metadata and was addressed by 4247c20f1. #25671 describes the broader inability of TreeArtifactValue to retain internal symlink identity. This reproduction already has the child metadata and fails when prefetch replaces a symlink present on disk.

Ordinary consumers of declared tree children supply a complete TreeArtifactValue through ActionInputMap. The same failure occurs through prefetchFiles with that provider. To exercise it in the test above, rename the method to prefetchFiles_treeFiles_directorySymlink_partiallyMaterializedWithTreeMetadata and add these imports:

```java
import static com.google.common.base.Preconditions.checkNotNull;

import com.google.devtools.build.lib.actions.ActionInputMap;
```

Then replace the prefetcher setup and call with:

```java
    ImmutableList<TreeFileArtifact> children = treeAndChildren.getSecond();
    TreeArtifactValue.Builder treeMetadata = TreeArtifactValue.newBuilder(tree);
    for (TreeFileArtifact child : children) {
      treeMetadata.putChild(child, checkNotNull(metadata.get(child)));
    }
    ActionInputMap inputMetadata = new ActionInputMap(children.size() + 1);
    inputMetadata.putTreeArtifact(tree, treeMetadata.build());
    AbstractActionInputPrefetcher prefetcher = createPrefetcher(cas);

    // The first alias child is already visible through the symlink. Preparing the next child's
    // directory must not make it disappear.
    wait(
        prefetcher.prefetchFiles(
            action,
            /* spawn= */ null,
            () -> children,
            inputMetadata,
            Priority.MEDIUM,
            Reason.INPUTS));
```

This version also fails at DirectoryTracker.setOutputPermissions for /exec/root/dir/alias/a on b353e093a7df2cc4a10a10faf3a702a3b3f1c951. The original reproduction remains a valid unresolved case that supplies only file metadata. This additional case isolates prefetch with the full tree metadata supplied by ordinary consumers.

