## Bevy version and features

`main` branch, commit 80240058748cf3c7fdcd79511f0525f464405a28

## What you did

Add this test in `crates/bevy_dev_tools/src/inspection/component_inspection.rs`:

```rust
    #[test]
    fn shortname_corrupts_values() {
        let mut world = World::new();
        world.init_resource::<AppTypeRegistry>();
        world
            .resource_mut::<AppTypeRegistry>()
            .write()
            .register::<Pathish>();

        let entity = world
            .spawn(Pathish {
                path: "bevy::prelude".to_string(),
            })
            .id();

        let settings = {
            let mut s = ComponentInspectionSettings::default();
            s.full_type_names = false;
            s
        };
        let inspection = world
            .inspect_component::<Pathish>(entity, settings)
            .unwrap();

        assert_eq!(
            inspection.value.unwrap(),
            "bevy_dev_tools::inspection::component_inspection::tests::Pathish {\n  path: \"bevy::prelude\",\n}"
        );
    }
```

running the test using the following command:

```shell
cargo test -p bevy_dev_tools shortname_corrupts_values
```

causes the test to fail (partial output):

```text
assertion `left == right` failed
  left: "Pathish {\n  path: prelude\",\n}"
 right: "bevy_dev_tools::inspection::component_inspection::tests::Pathish {\n  path: \"bevy::prelude\",\n}"
```

## What went wrong

As you can see from the `left` part of the failed assertion in the output above, using the short-name setting in `ComponentInspectionSettings` (i.e. `full_type_names` set to `false`), the string `bevy::prelude` (just a right-hand-value, not a left-hand-name) was truncated to `prelude` while it shouldn't have changed at all.

## Additional information

- See discussion in #25823 to learn more about the discovery of this bug.

