## How can Bevy's documentation be improved?

Currently, the module-level docs for `crates/bevy_reflect/src/display.rs` contain the following passage:

```rust
//! To recursively collapse all contained type paths to their "short names" (i.e. with no crate/module paths),
//! use [`disqualified::ShortName::from`] on the returned [`String`](alloc::string::String),
//! then use the [`Display`] implementation on [`ShortName`](disqualified::ShortName) for more concise output.
```

This leads developers to write code that applies `ShortName` to the entire output, including the values, instead of just shortening the left-hand values (it already happened in #25823).

