# Bevy Version

This issue is reproducible on versions `0.20.0-rc.1` and `0.19.*`, but does not appear to occur with `0.18.*`.

# Description

With some fonts, text nodes in flex layouts will wrap incorrectly, seemingly without updating the node's bounds in the layout. This behavior tends to only show for specific sizes, only a couple pixels in scale, and typically results in wrapped text being clipped.

The following showcase and example code both use the Montserrat font, but this issue happens with many other fonts too. It does not seems to appear for the default (Fira Mono) font.

# Showcase

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad6ab8c9-1ca7-441e-abb8-91cde9f129f8

# Repro code

The following repro example works for `0.20.0-rc.1` and `0.19.*`, and the font used can be found here: https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Montserrat;
```rust
use bevy::prelude::*;

fn main() {
    App::new()
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_systems(Startup, setup)
        .run();
}

fn setup(mut commands: Commands, assets: Res<AssetServer>) {
    commands.spawn((Camera::default(), Camera2d));

    commands
        .spawn(Node {
            width: percent(100),
            flex_direction: FlexDirection::Row,
            ..Default::default()
        })
        .with_child((
            Node {
                width: px(300),
                ..Default::default()
            },
            BackgroundColor(Color::WHITE),
        ))
        .with_child((
            Node {
                ..Default::default()
            },
            Text::new("{10, 20, 30}"),
            TextFont {
                font: FontSource::Handle(assets.load("Montserrat-Regular.ttf")),
                font_size: FontSize::Px(12.0),
                ..Default::default()
            },
            BackgroundColor(Color::BLACK),
        ));
}
```

