## Bevy version and features

- `0.20.0-dev`, upstream commit `383d525c841dd6d1c087b3b1b3b3c4b3248c5345`.
- `bevy_picking` default features; `InputPlugin`, `WindowPlugin`, `DefaultPickingPlugins`.

## What you did

Found while investigating missed taps and buttons staying pressed after lifting a finger in our Android/iOS game.

To isolate cancellation, inject `Started`, run one update, then inject `Canceled` and run another. Only `WindowEvent::TouchInput` is injected; the normal plugins handle touch conversion and picking. A small backend supplies a stationary hit target, without a renderer or phone.

Save this as `crates/bevy_picking/tests/touch_cancel.rs`:

```rust
use bevy_app::{App, PreUpdate};
use bevy_ecs::prelude::*;
use bevy_input::{touch::{TouchInput, TouchPhase}, InputPlugin};
use bevy_math::Vec2;
use bevy_picking::{
    backend::{HitData, PointerHits},
    events::{PointerCancel, PointerPress},
    pointer::{PointerId, PointerLocation},
    DefaultPickingPlugins, PickingSystems,
};
use bevy_window::{PrimaryWindow, WindowEvent, WindowPlugin};

#[test]
fn touch_cancellation_reaches_pressed_target() {
    let mut app = App::new();
    app.add_plugins((InputPlugin, WindowPlugin::default(), DefaultPickingPlugins))
        .add_systems(
            PreUpdate,
            (|pointers: Query<(&PointerId, &PointerLocation)>,
              window: Single<Entity, With<PrimaryWindow>>,
              mut hits: MessageWriter<PointerHits>| {
                for (id, location) in &pointers {
                    if location.location().is_some() {
                        hits.write(PointerHits::new(
                            *id,
                            vec![(*window, HitData::new(*window, 0., None, None))],
                            0.,
                        ));
                    }
                }
            }).in_set(PickingSystems::Backend),
        );
    app.update();
    let window = app.world_mut()
        .query_filtered::<Entity, With<PrimaryWindow>>()
        .single(app.world()).unwrap();
    for phase in [TouchPhase::Started, TouchPhase::Canceled] {
        app.world_mut().write_message(WindowEvent::TouchInput(TouchInput {
            window, phase, position: Vec2::splat(50.), force: None, id: 42,
        }));
        app.update();
    }
    assert_eq!(app.world().resource::<Messages<PointerPress>>().len(), 1);
    assert_eq!(app.world().resource::<Messages<PointerCancel>>().len(), 1);
}
```

```sh
cargo test -p bevy_picking --test touch_cancel
```

## What went wrong

- **Expected:** The target receives one `PointerPress` followed by one `PointerCancel`.
- **Actual:** The target receives one `PointerPress`, but no `PointerCancel`. The cancellation assertion fails.

```text
PointerPress: 1
PointerCancel:
  left:  0
  right: 1
```

## Additional information

- [Canceled pointers: excluded from hit reports](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/383d525c841dd6d1c087b3b1b3b3c4b3248c5345/crates/bevy_picking/src/hover.rs#L231-L245).
- [Cancel dispatch: current HoverMap](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/383d525c841dd6d1c087b3b1b3b3c4b3248c5345/crates/bevy_picking/src/events.rs#L1293-L1310).

AI tools assisted the investigation and reproduction test.

