## Bevy version and features

- `0.20.0-dev`, upstream commit `383d525c841dd6d1c087b3b1b3b3c4b3248c5345`.
- `bevy_picking` default features; `InputPlugin`, `WindowPlugin`, `DefaultPickingPlugins`.

## What you did

Found while debugging occasional missed taps and buttons remaining pressed in an Android/iOS Bevy game, including Android with three-button navigation.

Inject `Started` and `Ended` at the same position before one `app.update()`. The test also runs a control with an update between the two events. Only `WindowEvent::TouchInput` is injected; the normal plugins handle touch conversion and picking. A small backend supplies a stationary hit target, without a renderer or phone.

Save this as `crates/bevy_picking/tests/touch_same_frame.rs`:

```rust
//! Regression test for same-frame touch release.

use bevy_app::{App, PreUpdate};
use bevy_ecs::prelude::*;
use bevy_input::{
    touch::{TouchInput, TouchPhase},
    InputPlugin,
};
use bevy_math::Vec2;
use bevy_picking::{
    backend::{HitData, PointerHits},
    events::{PointerClick, PointerPress, PointerRelease},
    pointer::{PointerId, PointerLocation},
    DefaultPickingPlugins, PickingSystems,
};
use bevy_window::{PrimaryWindow, WindowEvent, WindowPlugin};

#[test]
fn touch_started_and_ended_in_one_frame() {
    // The next-frame control passes before the same-frame case fails.
    for separate_frames in [true, false] {
        let mut app = App::new();
        app.add_plugins((InputPlugin, WindowPlugin::default(), DefaultPickingPlugins))
            .add_systems(
                PreUpdate,
                (|pointers: Query<(&PointerId, &PointerLocation)>,
                  window: Single<Entity, With<PrimaryWindow>>,
                  mut hits: MessageWriter<PointerHits>| {
                    for (id, location) in &pointers {
                        if location.location().is_some() {
                            hits.write(PointerHits::new(
                                *id,
                                vec![(*window, HitData::new(*window, 0., None, None))],
                                0.,
                            ));
                        }
                    }
                })
                .in_set(PickingSystems::Backend),
            );
        app.update();
        let window = app
            .world_mut()
            .query_filtered::<Entity, With<PrimaryWindow>>()
            .single(app.world())
            .unwrap();
        for phase in [TouchPhase::Started, TouchPhase::Ended] {
            app.world_mut()
                .write_message(WindowEvent::TouchInput(TouchInput {
                    window,
                    phase,
                    position: Vec2::splat(50.),
                    force: None,
                    id: 42,
                }));
            if separate_frames || phase == TouchPhase::Ended {
                app.update();
            }
        }
        assert_eq!(
            [
                app.world().resource::<Messages<PointerPress>>().len(),
                app.world().resource::<Messages<PointerClick>>().len(),
                app.world().resource::<Messages<PointerRelease>>().len(),
            ],
            [1, 1, 1],
            "separate_frames={separate_frames}: Press, Click, Release",
        );
    }
}
```

```sh
cargo test -p bevy_picking --test touch_same_frame
```

## What went wrong

- **Expected:** Both cases emit one `PointerPress`, one `PointerClick` and one `PointerRelease`.
- **Actual:** The next-frame control passes. The same-frame case emits only `PointerPress`; `PointerClick` and `PointerRelease` are missing.

```text
separate_frames=true: [1, 1, 1]
separate_frames=false:
  left:  [1, 0, 0]
  right: [1, 1, 1]
```

## Additional information

- [Release dispatch: PreviousHoverMap](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/383d525c841dd6d1c087b3b1b3b3c4b3248c5345/crates/bevy_picking/src/events.rs#L1085-L1124). Related historical UI-focus fix: #7743.

