## Bevy version and features

- bevy 0.20
- `bevy = { version = "0.20", default-features = false, features = ["2d", "ui", "bevy_ui_widgets", "dynamic_linking"] }`
- Windows 10 & Windows 11

## What you did
After updating to bevy 0.20, I noticed that some Nodes which contain scroll areas get shifted when containing too many items.

The following snippet shows this issue:

```rust
use bevy::prelude::*;

fn main() {
    App::new()
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_systems(Startup, setup)
        .add_systems(Update, add_item)
        .run();
}

#[derive(Component, Clone, Default)]
struct Inner;

fn setup(mut commands: Commands) {
    commands.spawn(Camera2d);

    commands.spawn_scene(bsn! {
        Node {
            top: percent(30),
            left: percent(30),
            width: percent(40),
            height: percent(40),
            flex_direction: FlexDirection::Column,
            align_items: AlignItems::Stretch,
            justify_content: JustifyContent::Start,
            padding: UiRect::all(px(10))
        }
        Children [
            Inner
            Node {
                display: Display::Flex,
                flex_direction: FlexDirection::Column,
                align_items: AlignItems::Stretch,
                justify_content: JustifyContent::Start,
                overflow: Overflow::scroll_y(),
            }
        ]
        BackgroundColor(Color::srgb_u8(180, 180, 180))
    });
}

fn add_item(
    mut commands: Commands,
    scroll_area: Single<Entity, With<Inner>>,
    input: Res<ButtonInput<KeyCode>>,
) {
    if input.just_pressed(KeyCode::Space) {
        let scroll_area = scroll_area.into_inner();
        let item = commands
            .spawn_scene(bsn! {
                Text::new("Text")
                TextColor(Color::BLACK)
            })
            .id();

        commands.entity(scroll_area).add_child(item);
    }
}
```

After hitting Space a couple of times, the grey node starts moving down. This does not happen in 0.19.

The issue does not occur when the grey node itself has the overflow set.

