```

The above shows the minimal case, but I initially ran into this because it causes problems with Avian.
I built avian from source, and only removed the "bevy/multi_threading" line in the Cargo.toml
https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7cf00c3f-6143-4f48-a579-0f8d3771ed91

This is with multi_threading enabled
https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/59813045-d589-4e03-8de8-0b6f9046fc05

Frame 1 I pause physics, run my load function, then unpause the physics on frame 2, but on frame 3 avian runs delta_secs and gets the massive amount of time spent loading the scene in frame 1, rather than the time spent on frame 2 like it should.

It runs many physics frames at once, due to delta_secs being from the frame where the scene was loading (frame - 2), rather than the actual previous frame (frame - 1)

