#26171 exposed the problem with `JsonSchemaBevyType` that it returns wrong `schema_type`(`type`) for newtypes(tuplestructs with single field) + wrong `prefixItems`.

bevy_reflect serializes/deserializes newtypes as just literal value of internal type without any wrapping. Same thing applies for enum variants with tuples that consist from singular element
At same time bevy_reflect special-cases serialization/deserialization of Option<T> as either value itself or `null`, but scheme generation treats it as regular enum.


E.g. (from modified `examples/remote/server.rs`)
```rs
#[derive(Component, Reflect, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[reflect(Component, Serialize, Deserialize, Default)]
struct Cube(f32);

impl Default for Cube {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self(1.0)
    }
}
```
serializes into
```json
{"components":{"server::Cube":1.0},"errors":{}}
```
and spawned from
```json
{"jsonrpc":"2.0", "id":2,"method":"world.spawn_entity","params":{"components":{"server::Cube":1.0}}}
```
or 
```json
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"world.insert_components","params":{"entity":"507v0","components":{"server::Cube":1.0}}}
```
but scheme returns 
<details>

```json
      {
        "server::Cube": {
            "componentInfo": {
                "isSendAndSync": true,
                "mutable": true,
                "storageType": "Table"
            },
            "crateName": "server",
            "default": 1.0,
            "items": false,
            "kind": "TupleStruct",
            "modulePath": "server",
            "prefixItems": [
                {
                    "type": {
                        "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
                    }
                }
            ],
            "reflectTypes": [
                "Component",
                "Default",
                "Deserialize",
                "Serialize"
            ],
            "shortPath": "Cube",
            "type": "array",
            "typePath": "server::Cube"
        }
      }
```
</details>

which means that component's serialized form should look like that
```json
{"components":{"server::Cube":[1.0]}}
```
which is obviously not accepted
```json
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"world.insert_components","params":{"entity":"507v0","components":{"server::Cube":[1.0]}}}
```
```json
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"error":{"code":-23402,"message":"server::Cube is invalid: invalid type: sequence, expected f32"}}
```

Same problem exists with enums where one of the variants is tuple with single field, e.g.


```rs
#[derive(Component, Reflect, Serialize, Deserialize)] 
pub enum SpecialEnum {
    EmptyVariant,
    VariantA(f32),
    VariantB(f32, f32),
    VariantC{a: f32}
}
```
where ``TestType::VariantA(3.0)`` is represented by ``{"VariantA": 3.0}`` and ``TestType::VariantB(3.0, 4.0)`` is represented by ``{"VariantB": [3.0, 4.0]}``
but 
<details>

```json
{
  "crateName": "server",
  "kind": "Enum",
  "modulePath": "server",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "shortPath": "EmptyVariant",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::EmptyVariant"
    },
    {
      "items": false,
      "kind": "Tuple",
      "prefixItems": [
        {
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        }
      ],
      "shortPath": "VariantA",
      "type": "array",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::VariantA"
    },
    {
      "items": false,
      "kind": "Tuple",
      "prefixItems": [
        {
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        }
      ],
      "shortPath": "VariantB",
      "type": "array",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::VariantB"
    },
    {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "kind": "Struct",
      "properties": {
        "a": {
          "fieldIndex": 0,
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "a"
      ],
      "shortPath": "VariantC",
      "type": "object",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::VariantC"
    }
  ],
  "shortPath": "SpecialEnum",
  "type": "object",
  "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum"
}
```
</details>
suggests that ``SpecialEnum::VariantA(3.0)`` is represented by ``{ VariantA: [3.0]}`` which is wrong.
Also as additional note it returns wrong scheme for ``EmptyVariant`` as it doesn't enforce that it should be just string with "EmptyVariant" 

Problem gets worse for ``Option<T>`` as ``Option<f32>``
Where scheme returns 
<details>

```json
  "core::option::Option<f32>": {
    "crateName": "core",
    "default": null,
    "kind": "Enum",
    "modulePath": "core::option",
    "oneOf": [
      {
        "shortPath": "None",
        "typePath": "core::option::Option<f32>::None"
      },
      {
        "items": false,
        "kind": "Tuple",
        "prefixItems": [
          {
            "type": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
            }
          }
        ],
        "shortPath": "Some",
        "type": "array",
        "typePath": "core::option::Option<f32>::Some"
      }
    ],
    "reflectTypes": [
      "Default"
    ],
    "shortPath": "Option<f32>",
    "type": "object",
    "typePath": "core::option::Option<f32>"
  },
```
</details>

which is by itself half-broken and but also mean that from this point of view ``None`` is not re-presentable and ``Some(3.0)`` is represented by array with one element ``[3.0]``, which is wrong


# Suggested solution
There is exists pure JSON-schema solution for this problem, but the question of having enough ergonomics

I would suggest add: `Newtype` and `Option` variant into `SchemaKind` and adding `None` variant into `SchemaType` enum and represent those types:

For newtypes: 
<details>

```json
      {
        "server::Cube": {
            "componentInfo": {
                "isSendAndSync": true,
                "mutable": true,
                "storageType": "Table"
            },
            "crateName": "server",
            "default": 1.0,
            "items": false,
            "kind": "Newtype",
            "modulePath": "server",
            "oneOf": [
                {
                    "type": {
                        "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
                    }
                }
            ],
            "reflectTypes": [
                "Component",
                "Default",
                "Deserialize",
                "Serialize"
            ],
            "shortPath": "Cube",
            "typePath": "server::Cube"
        }
      }
```
</details>

For enums:
<details>

```json
{
  "crateName": "server",
  "kind": "Enum",
  "modulePath": "server",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "type": "string",
      "const": "EmptyVariant"
      "shortPath": "EmptyVariant",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::EmptyVariant"
    },
    {
      "items": false,
      "kind": "Newtype",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        }
      ],
      "shortPath": "VariantA",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::VariantA"
    },
    {
      "items": false,
      "kind": "Tuple",
      "prefixItems": [
        {
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        }
      ],
      "shortPath": "VariantB",
      "type": "array",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::VariantB"
    },
    {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "kind": "Struct",
      "properties": {
        "a": {
          "fieldIndex": 0,
          "type": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
          }
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "a"
      ],
      "shortPath": "VariantC",
      "type": "object",
      "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum::VariantC"
    }
  ],
  "shortPath": "SpecialEnum",
  "type": "object",
  "typePath": "server::SpecialEnum"
}
```
</details>

and for Option<T>

<details>

```json
  "core::option::Option<f32>": {
    "crateName": "core",
    "default": null,
    "kind": "Option",
    "modulePath": "core::option",
    "oneOf": [
      {
        "type": "null"
        "shortPath": "None",
        "typePath": "core::option::Option<f32>::None"
      },
      {
        "items": false,
        "type": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
        },
        "shortPath": "Some",
        "typePath": "core::option::Option<f32>::Some"
      }
    ],
    "reflectTypes": [
      "Default"
    ],
    "shortPath": "Option<f32>",
    "type": "object",
    "typePath": "core::option::Option<f32>"
  },
```
</details>

