`JsonSchemaBevyType` claims to follow https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-validation but have some glaring issues that prevents it from being compliant and at same time looks like trivially fixable

`$ref` should not be nested inside `type` AND `$ref` s are pointing to non-existent nodes:



E.g. For type

```rs
#[derive(Component, Reflect, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[reflect(Component, Serialize, Deserialize, Default)]
struct Cube(f32, f32);

impl Default for Cube {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self(1.0. 2.0)
    }
}
```

```json
"result": {
        ...
        "server::Cube": {
            "componentInfo": {
                "isSendAndSync": true,
                "mutable": true,
                "storageType": "Table"
            },
            "crateName": "server",
            "default": [
                1.0,
                2.0
            ],
            "items": false,
            "kind": "TupleStruct",
            "modulePath": "server",
            "prefixItems": [
                {
                    "type": {
                        "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": {
                        "$ref": "#/$defs/f32"
                    }
                }
            ],
            "reflectTypes": [
                "Component",
                "Default",
                "Deserialize",
                "Serialize"
            ],
            "shortPath": "Cube",
            "type": "array",
            "typePath": "server::Cube"
        },
}
```
should be 

```json
"result": {
        "$id": "urn:bevy-remote:registry"
        ...
        "server::Cube": {
            "componentInfo": {
                "isSendAndSync": true,
                "mutable": true,
                "storageType": "Table"
            },
            "crateName": "server",
            "default": [
                1.0,
                2.0
            ],
            "items": false,
            "kind": "TupleStruct",
            "modulePath": "server",
            "prefixItems": [
                {
                    "$ref": "#/f32"
                },
                {
                    "$ref": "#/f32"
                }
            ],
            "reflectTypes": [
                "Component",
                "Default",
                "Deserialize",
                "Serialize"
            ],
            "shortPath": "Cube",
            "type": "array",
            "typePath": "server::Cube"
        },
}
```

`$ref` should not be nested inside `type` as reference is by itself description of type + it wrong even on level of that ref is `object` while type should be just only string constant with name of type

 `"$ref": "#/$defs/ty_path"` s are pointing to non-existent nodes as there is literally no `"$defs" : {...}`.
# Suggested solution

Replace  `"$ref": "#/$defs/ty_path"` with `"$ref": "#/ty_name"`, so consumers of this scheme could create validator starting from `result` node(or find it by `"$id": "urn:bevy-remote:registry"`).

