body_text:
**Describe the bug**
When `Update` turns `View.AltScreen` off and returns `tea.Println(...)`, the line never appears. It is written while the terminal is still on the alt screen, and the next frame leaves the alt screen and takes the line with it. In v1 you could order the two with `tea.Sequence(tea.ExitAltScreen, tea.Println(...))`. v2 has no `ExitAltScreen` and nothing else to wait on.

- `cursedRenderer.render` only stores the view. The frame ticker writes it, alt-screen exit included, up to 1/fps later ([tea.go#L1437-L1466](https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea/blob/v2.1.0/tea.go#L1437-L1466)).
- `printLineMessage` goes to `cursedRenderer.insertAbove`, which writes to the terminal immediately ([cursed_renderer.go#L772-L828](https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea/blob/v2.1.0/cursed_renderer.go#L772-L828)).

This has the same root cause as #1736: there is no way to order `tea.Println` with the frame flush.

**To Reproduce**
```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"

    tea "charm.land/bubbletea/v2"
)

type model struct{ alt bool }

func (m model) Init() tea.Cmd { return nil }

func (m model) Update(msg tea.Msg) (tea.Model, tea.Cmd) {
    if k, ok := msg.(tea.KeyPressMsg); ok {
        switch k.String() {
        case "enter":
            m.alt = false
            return m, tea.Println("printed after leaving the alt screen")
        case "q":
            return m, tea.Quit
        }
    }
    return m, nil
}

func (m model) View() tea.View {
    v := tea.NewView(fmt.Sprintf("alt=%v  enter: leave the alt screen and print · q: quit", m.alt))
    v.AltScreen = m.alt
    return v
}

func main() {
    if _, err := tea.NewProgram(model{alt: true}).Run(); err != nil {
        fmt.Println(err)
    }
}
```
Run it and press Enter.

**Expected behavior**
`printed after leaving the alt screen` appears above the inline view.

**Actual behavior**
Only the inline view appears. If the same `tea.Println` is returned from a `tea.Tick(50*time.Millisecond, …)` message instead, the line appears.

**Fix**
#1741 (flush the queued view before `insertAbove`) fixes this. I ran the repro above in tmux 3 times against each build. On v2.1.0 the line printed 0 of 3 times. With #1741 (fc7e01f) it printed 3 of 3 times. `go test ./...` passes on that branch.

#1804, as described, makes `Println` a no-op while the alt screen is active. That would still drop this line, because the renderer is still on the alt screen when the print arrives.

**Setup**
- charm.land/bubbletea/v2 v2.1.0
- macOS 26, tmux; also seen under asciinema

